<keyword_placement>
Primary keywords:
- Do NOT change any primary keyword already present in skeleton.

Secondary keywords (coverage + uniqueness):
- Only use exact strings from context.seo.secondaryKeywords.
- Each secondary keyword MUST appear in exactly ONE section.keywords[] across the whole outline.
- No secondary keyword may appear in more than one section.keywords[].

How to apply:
- Use op="push" to add secondary keywords into the chosen section.keywords array.
- Do not add keywords to sections where it harms intent (pick the best-fitting section).

Example:
context.seo.secondaryKeywords = [
  "eye cream for puffiness",
  "daily moisturizer for sensitive skin",
  "hydration for dry skin",
  "under eye hydration",
  "lightweight moisturizer"
]

Edits:
{
  "edits": [
    { "op": "push", "path": "sections.2.keywords", "value": "under eye hydration" },
    { "op": "push", "path": "sections.3.keywords", "value": "daily moisturizer for sensitive skin" },
    { "op": "push", "path": "sections.1.keywords", "value": "hydration for dry skin" },
    { "op": "push", "path": "sections.5.keywords", "value": "eye cream for puffiness" },
    { "op": "push", "path": "sections.6.keywords", "value": "lightweight moisturizer" }
  ]
}
</keyword_placement>
